{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1180132-prosecution-for-crimes-by-nimbus","id":1180132,"title":"prosecution for Crimes by nimbus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-28T05:38:11-08:00","id":1180132,"title":"prosecution for Crimes by nimbus","content":"A thought occurred to me recently. Mage society does not seem geared to protect sleepers on an individual level from abuse by mages aside from obvious gross violations. individual mages may act to protect acquaintances friends etc but I don't get the impression that Lex Magica is much concerned with such things. However abusing sleepers tends to cause wisdom to drop and as wisdom drops the effects of the long term Nimbus spread. Has anyone ever played with the idea of the local consilium bringing charges against a powerful Mage because his long-term Nimbus is causing so many issues throughout the city, and indirectly punishing him for his abuses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T08:09:01-08:00","id":1180166,"title":"","content":"Your Nimbus doesn't punish you, it's part of you, even if it's semi-autonomous, and it also doesn't leak indiscriminately throughout a region but instead via your Sympathetic connections.<br /> <br /> That said, it could possibly interfere with the interests of other Mages, but I doubt it would really be a crime since typically it's not deliberate. More likely it would be the kind of thing that kicks off a feud or results in a trip to the Mage version of a small claims court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T08:32:34-08:00","id":1180171,"title":"","content":"I understand that the Nimbus does not damage the Mage itself but I was thinking about something along these lines: the powerful moros, bit of a bastard, not averse to occasionally experimenting on people or wiping them out for convenience sake maintains and identity as upper management in some company or other downtown. He maintains an office there and also occasionally rides the subway to work partly to look for subjects partly to look for ghosts. His wisdom has dropped down to about 3. At this point I would expect his coworkers for instance to be experiencing more than the occasional haunting. More than you would usually expect to see scattered among those coworkers. The subway is a bit more likely to break down or in the show hauntings as well. The powers-that-be among Mages which end to lookout for things like that try to figure out why these things are happening more frequently than they should. At some point someone starts looking to see what connections are made and they follow sympathy back to the Mage and realize many of these issues are tied to him. The Guardians at least I would think would have a problem with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T06:07:12-08:00","id":1180401,"title":"","content":"Something else to remember is that the effects of a Mage's Long-Term Nimbus don't have said Mage's Nimbus stamped on them. A magical disease outbreak by a Thyrsus doesn't have ol' Hawk's Signature Nimbus on it, even if it was triggered by it. There isn't really a way to distinguish between something triggered by a Nimbus and something that just happens by coincidence. Heck, the very idea of coincidence gets funky when the Awakened are around.<br /> <br /> Plus, Mages tend to like it when odd stuff happens; it's Mystery fuel. If anything, I can see this as a part of the incentive for forming a cabal, since cabals share a common symbolism and common sympathies. It might make it significantly more likely for their shared Obsessions to appear to them.<br /> <br /> All in all, this feels more like something the Awakened would encourage, not discourage. At least privately, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T10:02:49-08:00","id":1180446,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, especially the indirectness of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:18:59-08:00","id":1180488,"title":"","content":"I realize the long term and signiture nimbus are not the same, but I figured that at some point, if weird things keep happening in certain area, some mage or other would use Space magic to see what associations they have in common.<br /> It does make sense that some mages would rather study the long term effects than complain about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T14:02:36-08:00","id":1180499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1180132-prosecution-for-crimes-by-nimbus?p=1180488#post1180488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does make sense that some mages would rather study the long term effects than complain about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if you're a Guardian do both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}